<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="{{ csp }}">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Spatial study evidence — {{ study.definition.study_id }}</title>
<style>{{ css }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to evidence</a>
<header class="study-header">
<p class="scope">Synthetic / exploratory / unobserved / non-causal / not sales</p>
<p class="eyebrow">Schema-v10 paired study · rule baseline and bounded cognition evidence</p>
<h1>Study verdict</h1>
<p class="study-name"><bdi dir="auto">{{ study.definition.study_id }}</bdi> · <bdi dir="auto">{{ study.city.name }}</bdi></p>
<dl class="verdicts">
<dt>Protocol size</dt><dd>{{ study.seeds|length }} seeds · {{ study.evidence_tier }}</dd>
<dt>Opportunity structure</dt><dd>{{ study.opportunity_classification }}</dd>
<dt>Response assumptions</dt><dd>{{ study.response_assumption_classification }}</dd>
<dt>A/A invariant</dt><dd>{{ study.a_a_status }}</dd>
</dl>
<p class="warning">Intervals describe deterministic simulator seed variation, not population confidence, observed behavior, or a campaign effect.</p>
</header>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
<section class="baseline" aria-labelledby="baseline-heading">
<h2 id="baseline-heading">Rule baseline</h2>
<p>Statistics below are treatment minus control on attention evidence and the rule-owned baseline only. Purchase intention is an uncalibrated rule-owned proxy, not a purchase probability, a sale, or a transaction.</p>
<p>Effect scope of the separate cognition track is <bdi dir="auto">bounded-signals-v1</bdi>. That track is not in this table.</p>
<div class="table-region" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="statistics-caption">
<table class="statistics"><caption id="statistics-caption">Rule-baseline and attention statistics ({{ study.statistics|length }} metrics)</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Metric and sources</th><th scope="col">Seeds</th><th scope="col">Mean paired difference</th><th scope="col">Direction</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for statistic in study.statistics %}<tr>
<th scope="row"><bdi dir="auto">{{ statistic.metric_key }}</bdi></th>
<td>{{ statistic.n_seeds }}</td>
<td>{{ statistic.mean_paired_difference }}</td>
<td><bdi dir="auto">{{ statistic.direction }}</bdi></td>
</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
</div>
</section>
<section class="cognition" aria-labelledby="cognition-heading">
<h2 id="cognition-heading">Bounded cognition evidence</h2>
<p>Provider-dependent exploratory evidence, not observed behavior, and not validated psychology. This section is not a treatment effect, not a sales lift, not a conversion probability, and not a validated prediction.</p>
<p>Frozen schema-v10 replay reapplies saved signals and performs no provider call. Hashes detect accidental change. These artifacts are unsigned.</p>
<p>A profile revision is the hash below when present. This study receipt does not store a model ID.</p>
{% for row in cognition_rows %}
<article class="pair" aria-labelledby="cognition-{{ row.seed }}-{{ row.arm }}">
<h3 id="cognition-{{ row.seed }}-{{ row.arm }}">Seed {{ row.seed }} · {{ row.arm }}</h3>
<dl class="ledger">
<dt>provenance classification</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.classification }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>mode</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.mode }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>effect scope</dt><dd>bounded-signals-v1</dd>
<dt>profile revision</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.profile_revision }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>prompt contract sha256</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.prompt_contract_sha256 }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>result schema sha256</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.result_schema_contract_sha256 }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>influence policy sha256</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.influence_policy_sha256 }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>funded coverage</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.funded_coverage }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>source counts</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.sources }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>fallback counts</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.fallbacks }}</bdi></dd>
<dt>category counts</dt><dd><bdi dir="auto">{{ row.categories }}</bdi></dd>
</dl>
</article>
{% endfor %}
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="limitations-heading">
<h2 id="limitations-heading">Limitations</h2>
<p>These are synthetic, exploratory model comparisons: unobserved, non-causal and not sales. Cognition provenance is not subtracted. No cognition treatment-minus-control statistic is reported.</p>
</section>
</main>
<footer>Spatial study HTML v2 · synthetic-study-not-observed-or-causal-effect</footer>
</body>
</html>
